/**
 * @page gui_doc Comfort Select GUI - Interactive Frontend
 *
 * @section gui_overview 1. GUI Frontend Architecture Overview
 *
 * The **Comfort Select GUI Frontend** is an interactive desktop application built using **GTKmm-4**.
 * It implements a highly structured, signal-driven **Model-View-ViewModel (MVVM)** architectural pattern.
 * This completely decouples frontend presentation and rendering loops from backend logic, ensuring that
 * heavy operations like database transactions, USB polling, or math calculations do not freeze the UI main loop.
 *
 * ---
 *
 * @section mvvm_structure 2. MVVM Component Breakdown
 *
 * The frontend is organized into clear presentation layers:
 *
 * @subsection mvvm_view A. View (Interactive Widgets)
 * Handles layout rendering, stylesheet applications, user interaction event handling, and drawing charts.
 * - **MainWindow**: Manages the main GTK application window derivation, loaded dynamically from GTK builder XML blueprints (`main_window.ui`). It coordinates widget signal bindings.
 *   - See: libscale::MainWindow
 * - **TrendGraph**: Custom Cairo-drawn time-series widget with automatic bounds scaling, grid lines, and interactive hover-popover labels.
 *   - See: libscale::TrendGraph
 * - **HistoryRow**: Custom smooth-scrolling list item row widget designed for GTK ListView dynamic column mappings.
 *   - See: libscale::HistoryRow
 *
 * @subsection mvvm_viewmodel B. ViewModel (Presentation State)
 * Bridges the backend `HealthManager` with the user interface components.
 * - **DashboardViewModel**: Acts as the single source of truth for the active display data. It manages date filtering, range slider percentages, and preset intervals (30 days, 90 days, 1 year). When the active selection changes, it emits Glib signals to notify widgets to redraw.
 *   - See: libscale::DashboardViewModel
 *
 * @subsection mvvm_settings C. Settings Persistence
 * - **ISettingsManager**: Interface for loading and persisting desktop UI states (window width, height, maximized state, dark mode preference, unit system metric/imperial, and last active user profile).
 * - **JsonSettingsManager**: Concrete implementation persisting layout settings to a local JSON configuration file.
 *   - See: libscale::ISettingsManager, libscale::JsonSettingsManager
 *
 * ---
 *
 * @section ui_assets 3. UI Assets & Dynamic Styling
 *
 * - **main_window.ui**: Blueprint interface file loaded dynamically by Gtk::Builder to construct the widget hierarchy.
 * - **style.css**: Application-wide style sheets providing cohesive dark-theme glassmorphism, responsive colors, and hover transitions.
 */
